; i32 compares. Ordered ones are a 32-bit subtraction whose flags are
; branched on: subd on the low halves, then SBCBR (sbcb/sbca on the high
; halves and a branch). Z is only the high half's, so GT, LE, HI and LS
; become the other conditions with the operands swapped or the constant
; moved by one. Equality compares are left to the generic expansion.

